# `SEQUENCE-CONTAINMENT-SCOPE`: the OBJECT rule for `in=`. Its value domain under this
# genre is a `fragment` or an `operand` id and nothing else, so a lifeline id
# there is a specific mistake — the author has the relation right and the
# object wrong — and the diagnostic says so before it lists the acceptors.
#
# `operand in=` is narrower still: a compartment belongs to a FRAGMENT, never
# to another compartment, so both wrong objects get their own sentence.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
lifeline s "S"
fragment f "F" type=alt
operand o "O" in=f
message c -> s "names a lifeline" in=c
message c -> s "names nothing declared" in=nowhere
state c "X" in=c
operand p "names an operand" in=o
operand q "names a lifeline" in=c
fragment g "names a lifeline" type=opt in=s
